WEBVTT

00:00:04.046 --> 00:00:05.114
Ah.

00:00:06.248 --> 00:00:08.150
(cockroach chattering)

00:00:12.955 --> 00:00:15.024
- ♪
- (chatters)

00:00:16.058 --> 00:00:17.526
(yells)

00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:19.328
(grunts, chatters)

00:00:19.428 --> 00:00:21.063
("Freedom" by Pitbull playing)

00:00:21.163 --> 00:00:23.832
♪ Let's be free, baby,
and cruise the world ♪

00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:25.800
♪ Are you with it, girl?

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.272
♪ I'm free to do what I want
and have a good time... ♪

00:00:30.372 --> 00:00:32.475
(laughing)

00:00:32.575 --> 00:00:34.709
Thank you. Look at everyone.

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:37.812
Yes. We are having
a good time, right?

00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:40.615
(singing along):
♪ I'm free to do what I want

00:00:40.715 --> 00:00:42.418
♪ And have a good time...

00:00:42.518 --> 00:00:44.886
(whooping)

00:00:45.955 --> 00:00:48.623
(laughs)
No, I love you.

00:00:48.723 --> 00:00:51.626
Thank you, my beautiful army.

00:00:51.726 --> 00:00:55.030
Maxime's back, baby! (laughs)

00:00:55.131 --> 00:00:57.366
(cheering)

00:00:57.466 --> 00:00:59.168
And a special <i>merci beaucoup</i>

00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:02.071
to everyone who helped me
break out of AVL prison.

00:01:02.171 --> 00:01:04.373
Todd and Linda, where are you?
Where are you?

00:01:04.473 --> 00:01:05.807
Yes. For distracting the guards.

00:01:05.907 --> 00:01:08.377
<i>- Oh, très magnifique.</i>
- (whooping)

00:01:08.477 --> 00:01:11.080
- (laughs) Now, silence!
- (cheering and whooping stop)

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.416
We must make Gru suffer
for arresting me.

00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:15.985
(laughs)

00:01:16.085 --> 00:01:19.221
And what better way
than to take away from him

00:01:19.321 --> 00:01:21.090
his precious little baby?

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.626
Oh, I want to take that baby!
(laughs)

00:01:23.725 --> 00:01:25.793
- (gasps, exclaims)
- (whistling, cheering)

00:01:25.894 --> 00:01:28.464
- Oh, Maxime.
- No, no, wait, wait.

00:01:28.564 --> 00:01:29.831
Not Maxime.

00:01:29.932 --> 00:01:32.901
What if I start going
by Cockroach Man?

00:01:33.002 --> 00:01:35.904
Huh? Little on the nose,
but it is very clear, huh?

00:01:36.005 --> 00:01:37.573
- It's good, no?
- (scoffs)

00:01:37.672 --> 00:01:39.807
I'm not calling you
that stupid name,

00:01:39.908 --> 00:01:42.411
but I love this evil plan.

00:01:42.511 --> 00:01:44.013
Well, Gru has it coming.

00:01:44.113 --> 00:01:46.949
He humiliated me
in front of the whole school.

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:50.152
I had my trophy and everything.

00:01:50.252 --> 00:01:53.556
- But now the game begins!
- (cockroach exclaims)

00:01:53.656 --> 00:01:55.624
He runs and hides
like the mouse,

00:01:55.723 --> 00:01:58.994
and we find him like the cat!

00:01:59.094 --> 00:02:01.063
Game on.

00:02:03.199 --> 00:02:04.133
(Ron chuckles)

00:02:04.233 --> 00:02:06.502
- Stoppa. Stoppa.
- (chuckling continues)

00:02:06.602 --> 00:02:09.471
Stoppa. Stoppa.

00:02:09.572 --> 00:02:11.307
(exclaims in Minionese)

00:02:11.407 --> 00:02:13.908
- Stoppa!
- (laughing)

00:02:14.009 --> 00:02:17.346
♪ Okay, we've got Chet's famous
super cheesy scrambled eggs ♪

00:02:17.446 --> 00:02:19.648
- (Lucy humming)
- ♪ And Blanche's famous bacon

00:02:19.747 --> 00:02:21.517
♪ That spells your name.

00:02:21.617 --> 00:02:23.586
Here you go...

00:02:23.686 --> 00:02:25.588
Britney.

00:02:25.688 --> 00:02:26.788
Wait.

00:02:26.888 --> 00:02:29.558
I can't say my name is Britney.

00:02:29.658 --> 00:02:31.427
That would be a lie.

00:02:31.527 --> 00:02:32.760
Yes.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:35.464
But we aren't "stupposed"
to lie.

00:02:35.564 --> 00:02:37.099
Don't think of it as lying.

00:02:37.199 --> 00:02:39.702
Think of it as
high-stakes pretending.

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:41.903
Well, I'm not going to.

00:02:42.004 --> 00:02:44.906
- Ah, just a little white lie.
- Nope.

00:02:45.007 --> 00:02:48.110
Agnes, as your father,
I command you to lie.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:48.911
No.

00:02:49.011 --> 00:02:50.913
- Yes, lie.
- Mm-mm.

00:02:51.013 --> 00:02:53.983
You are walking on thin ice,
little lady.

00:02:54.083 --> 00:02:54.882
Hmph.

00:02:54.984 --> 00:02:56.318
(Gru Jr. giggling, munching)

00:02:56.418 --> 00:02:58.853
Why can't you be more like
your sister Edith?

00:02:58.954 --> 00:03:00.723
She lies all the time.

00:03:00.822 --> 00:03:02.857
- No, I don't.
- See? See?

00:03:02.958 --> 00:03:04.593
She's lying right now.

00:03:04.693 --> 00:03:05.860
Beautifully, I might add.

00:03:05.961 --> 00:03:07.229
LUCY:
Okay, you guys.

00:03:07.329 --> 00:03:09.031
This is our first big day
in Mayflower,

00:03:09.131 --> 00:03:11.500
and I say we make it
a great one.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.135
Right, Chet Jr.?

00:03:13.235 --> 00:03:14.769
- Woo-hoo! Mayflower!
- (Gru Jr. squeals excitedly)

00:03:14.869 --> 00:03:16.572
Yeah! Woo-hoo!

00:03:16.672 --> 00:03:18.140
We're gonna be late for karate.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.841
- And you have to get Margo
to school. -Ah.

00:03:19.942 --> 00:03:21.644
- (Margo groans)
- EDITH: It's gonna be awesome.

00:03:21.744 --> 00:03:23.112
- (unenthusiastically): Yay.
- Hey.

00:03:23.212 --> 00:03:26.615
You just have to put yourself
out there, and I promise,

00:03:26.715 --> 00:03:28.917
Mayflower will love
Chet Cunningham.

00:03:29.018 --> 00:03:31.320
Well, they're gonna love him
just as much as I do.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.655
GRU:
Mm.

00:03:32.755 --> 00:03:34.056
And you, little man,
are gonna have

00:03:34.156 --> 00:03:35.857
so much fun
with your daddy today.

00:03:35.958 --> 00:03:37.693
(smacking lips)

00:03:37.792 --> 00:03:40.663
Yep, just you and Dada.

00:03:40.763 --> 00:03:42.665
Come on, say it. "Dada."

00:03:42.765 --> 00:03:45.067
"Dada."

00:03:46.335 --> 00:03:47.902
(blows raspberry)

00:03:48.003 --> 00:03:50.439
Gonna be a fun day.

00:03:50.539 --> 00:03:53.242
♪

00:03:54.777 --> 00:03:57.812
(takes deep breath)

00:04:01.684 --> 00:04:04.953
- (Minions grunting rapidly)
- ("Hot for Teacher" playing)

00:04:06.922 --> 00:04:08.924
(grunting, speaking Minionese)

00:04:09.024 --> 00:04:10.793
- Okay.
- (drill whirring)

00:04:10.892 --> 00:04:12.494
(speaking Minionese)

00:04:12.594 --> 00:04:14.330
(laughing)

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:17.533
- Thanks a lot, guys.
- (chuckles, speaks Minionese)

00:04:17.633 --> 00:04:20.202
(speaking Minionese)

00:04:20.302 --> 00:04:21.804
(laughs)

00:04:21.903 --> 00:04:23.806
MAN:
All right.

00:04:23.905 --> 00:04:25.808
- Thanks, hon. Bye.
- Bye.

00:04:25.907 --> 00:04:28.477
Look, Margo. Neighbors.

00:04:28.577 --> 00:04:30.212
Hello!

00:04:30.312 --> 00:04:31.480
Hmm?

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.681
Come on.

00:04:32.781 --> 00:04:34.516
You got this, Chet.

00:04:34.616 --> 00:04:36.151
(shudders)

00:04:36.251 --> 00:04:39.555
I'm your new neighbor,
Chet Cunningham.

00:04:39.655 --> 00:04:41.090
Uh-huh. Perry Prescott.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:45.594
So, what, uh, brings you
to the neighborhood, Chet?

00:04:45.694 --> 00:04:48.030
Well, uh...

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:49.864
(gasps)
Solar panels.

00:04:49.965 --> 00:04:52.900
That's it. I sell solar panels.

00:04:53.001 --> 00:04:55.637
Have you joined
the solar revolution?

00:04:55.738 --> 00:04:57.439
Yeah, no.

00:04:57.539 --> 00:04:59.408
Uh, I think I'm good.

00:04:59.508 --> 00:05:00.609
Good to know.

00:05:00.709 --> 00:05:02.444
So, uh, what do you do, Perry?

00:05:02.544 --> 00:05:04.179
I own Prescott Motors,

00:05:04.279 --> 00:05:07.882
the largest auto dealer
in the state.

00:05:07.983 --> 00:05:10.486
Wow. That's impressive.

00:05:10.586 --> 00:05:12.588
This is my daughter Margo.

00:05:12.688 --> 00:05:13.822
Bree, Dad.

00:05:13.922 --> 00:05:15.591
GRU:
Ah, yes.

00:05:15.691 --> 00:05:17.292
Yes. Did I say "Margo"?

00:05:17.393 --> 00:05:19.728
It's funny because
I was thinking...

00:05:19.828 --> 00:05:21.163
I was thinking about a fish

00:05:21.263 --> 00:05:23.298
I once had as a pet named Margo,

00:05:23.399 --> 00:05:27.703
who lived in the pond
and, uh, then died.

00:05:27.803 --> 00:05:29.705
(stammers softly)

00:05:29.805 --> 00:05:32.241
Anyway, I, uh...

00:05:32.341 --> 00:05:36.111
I am about to take Bree
to school for her first day.

00:05:36.211 --> 00:05:39.481
Yeah, I was about to take Poppy
to school, so...

00:05:39.581 --> 00:05:41.550
Poppy. Hello, Poppy.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.619
That's a fun name to say.

00:05:43.719 --> 00:05:45.421
You want to carpool with us?

00:05:45.521 --> 00:05:46.922
No.

00:05:47.022 --> 00:05:48.857
You can be friends with Bree.

00:05:48.957 --> 00:05:50.159
Right, Bree?

00:05:50.259 --> 00:05:52.761
You don't have any friends.

00:05:52.861 --> 00:05:54.329
(Margo chuckles awkwardly)

00:05:55.497 --> 00:05:58.300
Well, love the chitchat, Chet,
but she's got school,

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.270
and I'm meeting some pals
over at the country club, so...

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:03.238
Ooh, country club.
That sounds like a lot of fun.

00:06:03.338 --> 00:06:05.507
If I were ever invited
to a country club,

00:06:05.607 --> 00:06:10.112
(chuckles): I am sure
that I would love it.

00:06:11.079 --> 00:06:12.981
Yeah, well, we really
have to get going,

00:06:13.081 --> 00:06:14.450
- so nice meeting you, Chet.
- (engine starts)

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:16.351
(over stereo):
♪ I'm too sexy...

00:06:16.452 --> 00:06:17.719
Okay, cool.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:21.990
Anytime you want to hang out,
just hit me up with a text.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.959
He's gonna text me.

00:06:24.059 --> 00:06:26.128
That was painful.

00:06:26.829 --> 00:06:29.131
♪

00:06:30.432 --> 00:06:33.235
You'll see, by lunchtime,
you will have forgotten

00:06:33.335 --> 00:06:36.071
all about your old,
lousy friends.

00:06:36.171 --> 00:06:38.974
Mm, not so sure about that.

00:06:43.212 --> 00:06:44.680
(students chattering, laughing)

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:46.381
(bicycle bell dings)

00:06:47.416 --> 00:06:48.684
(sighs)

00:06:48.784 --> 00:06:50.719
Hey, honey, you got this.

00:06:50.819 --> 00:06:52.888
You are smart. You are funny.

00:06:52.988 --> 00:06:54.958
What's there to worry about, right?

00:06:55.057 --> 00:06:57.559
They're gonna love you.

00:06:58.627 --> 00:07:00.395
Thanks, Gru.

00:07:01.864 --> 00:07:03.565
Buh-bye.

00:07:04.968 --> 00:07:07.603
Oh, please let them love you.

00:07:07.703 --> 00:07:09.638
(sighs)

00:07:09.738 --> 00:07:11.173
(gasps)

00:07:12.508 --> 00:07:14.476
Hey, Poppy.

